1
00:00:01,560 --> 00:00:03,520
Wealth, Fame, Power.

2
00:00:03,840 --> 00:00:05,937
Gold Roger, the King of the Pirates,

3
00:00:06,020 --> 00:00:08,717
obtained this and everything
else the world had to offer.

4
00:00:08,800 --> 00:00:11,880
His dying words drove
countless souls to the seas.

5
00:00:12,300 --> 00:00:13,680
You want my treasure?

6
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:15,180
You can have it.

7
00:00:15,320 --> 00:00:17,997
I left everything I gathered
together in one place.

8
00:00:18,080 --> 00:00:19,980
Now you just have to find it.

9
00:00:20,160 --> 00:00:22,697
These words lured men to
the Grand Line in pursuits

10
00:00:22,780 --> 00:00:25,197
of dreams greater than
they ever dared to imagine.

11
00:00:25,280 --> 00:00:28,340
This is the time known
as the Great Pirate Era.

12
00:00:32,260 --> 00:00:37,600
Come forward and bring us along,
all your hopes and dreams,

13
00:00:37,860 --> 00:00:43,040
together we will find a greeting
that we're looking for, one piece.

14
00:00:47,360 --> 00:00:49,997
The hump is left behind.

15
00:00:50,080 --> 00:00:52,857
It'll only slow us down.

16
00:00:52,940 --> 00:00:55,637
Your heart will be your guide.

17
00:00:55,720 --> 00:00:58,717
Raise the sails and take the helm.

18
00:00:58,800 --> 00:01:01,637
That legendary place.

19
00:01:01,720 --> 00:01:04,217
That the end of the map reveals.

20
00:01:04,300 --> 00:01:07,337
Is only legendary.

21
00:01:07,420 --> 00:01:10,900
Till someone proves it real.

22
00:01:12,180 --> 00:01:14,857
Through it all, through all the trouble.

23
00:01:14,940 --> 00:01:16,557
And through the heartache.

24
00:01:16,640 --> 00:01:17,597
And through the pain.

25
00:01:17,680 --> 00:01:20,497
I know that I will be there.

26
00:01:20,580 --> 00:01:22,200
To stand by you.

27
00:01:23,080 --> 00:01:25,257
Just like I know you'll stand by me.

28
00:01:25,340 --> 00:01:28,157
So come forward and pray along.

29
00:01:28,240 --> 00:01:30,337
All your hopes and dreams.

30
00:01:30,420 --> 00:01:33,197
Together we will find everything.

31
00:01:33,280 --> 00:01:34,940
That we will explore.

32
00:01:37,480 --> 00:01:38,697
There is silence.

33
00:01:38,780 --> 00:01:39,957
For you.

34
00:01:40,040 --> 00:01:43,020
If you want to be my friend?

35
00:01:44,040 --> 00:01:44,940
We are!

36
00:01:45,320 --> 00:01:47,540
We are on the cruise!

37
00:01:48,180 --> 00:01:49,080
We are!

38
00:01:59,800 --> 00:02:01,720
Praise Alabasta!

39
00:02:04,040 --> 00:02:04,870
Yay!

40
00:02:14,340 --> 00:02:16,440
Take care on your voyage!

41
00:02:20,960 --> 00:02:24,680
Didi-chan looked like she was
having a fine time, didn't she?

42
00:02:25,040 --> 00:02:27,417
She must have been feeling
like a pirate again.

43
00:02:27,500 --> 00:02:30,677
Just when I thought she'd started
to act like a real princess.

44
00:02:30,760 --> 00:02:32,060
Yes, this is Head.

45
00:02:32,780 --> 00:02:38,280
We will now proceed to escort
the Nefaltari safe to Mary Jo's.

46
00:02:41,800 --> 00:02:42,840
Princess Vivi!

47
00:02:43,200 --> 00:02:45,259
Please get down from there at once!

48
00:02:47,680 --> 00:02:50,700
The ocean breeze feels so wonderful.

49
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:55,640
Princess Vivi!

50
00:02:55,920 --> 00:02:59,437
What if a monstrous bird were to sweep
down from the sky and abduct you?

51
00:02:59,520 --> 00:03:02,737
What if there were a sniper
lurking in wait to take your life?

52
00:03:02,820 --> 00:03:04,879
What if a meteor fell from the sky?

53
00:03:05,440 --> 00:03:08,146
Princess Vivi traveled
with pirates, remember?

54
00:03:09,300 --> 00:03:11,537
There are marines
standing right next to us.

55
00:03:11,620 --> 00:03:13,020
You worry too much.

56
00:03:14,240 --> 00:03:15,320
Cough. Cough.

57
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:18,848
Please do not strain
yourself, Your Majesty.

58
00:03:19,080 --> 00:03:22,374
If you are feeling unwell,
we can turn back at any time.

59
00:03:23,960 --> 00:03:25,220
No, I am alright.

60
00:03:27,060 --> 00:03:29,980
Ever since that day when I met Nico Robin,

61
00:03:30,140 --> 00:03:33,817
I've had some questions that I would
like to ask of the world government.

62
00:03:33,900 --> 00:03:36,340
Is this about the poneglyphs?

63
00:03:37,680 --> 00:03:43,680
Too many enemies in the way of my dream I
must attend this reverie no matter what.

64
00:03:44,300 --> 00:03:47,737
And if fate will allow it I would
very much like to know what it was.

65
00:03:47,820 --> 00:03:51,880
That the king of the house of
Nefertari did to the world long ago.

66
00:04:02,980 --> 00:04:05,700
Ma! Ma! Ma! Ma! Ma!

67
00:04:06,900 --> 00:04:10,160
Honestly, will you stop
this madness, Princess Vivi?

68
00:04:11,140 --> 00:04:13,180
Father, how are you feeling?

69
00:04:13,900 --> 00:04:16,280
Hmm, I have certainly felt better.

70
00:04:16,840 --> 00:04:18,677
Perhaps I do not have much longer.

71
00:04:18,760 --> 00:04:21,289
If only my daughter
were to take a husband.

72
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:28,602
We have received a veritable
mountain of photographs from suitors.

73
00:04:29,940 --> 00:04:31,360
Turn them all away.

74
00:04:37,920 --> 00:04:40,917
Congratulations on your recent
coronation, your majesty!

75
00:04:41,000 --> 00:04:44,260
We hope you find
everything to your liking.

76
00:04:45,220 --> 00:04:49,037
This hotel was built for the
sole use of royal personages.

77
00:04:49,120 --> 00:04:52,380
on their journey to the
reverie once every four years.

78
00:04:54,080 --> 00:04:57,040
It is not, not, not bad.

79
00:04:57,300 --> 00:04:58,653
Isn't that right, dear?

80
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,547
Well, it is fairly ordinary.

81
00:05:00,760 --> 00:05:04,525
This view of Gold Roger's execution
platform is charming enough.

82
00:05:04,900 --> 00:05:06,777
Well, then have a wonderful stay.

83
00:05:06,860 --> 00:05:08,154
We hope you rest well.

84
00:05:08,600 --> 00:05:09,430
Yes, yes.

85
00:05:09,860 --> 00:05:13,036
Be gone from my sight, you
irritating pieces of trash.

86
00:05:13,360 --> 00:05:14,190
King Stella!

87
00:05:22,220 --> 00:05:25,620
In countries the world over,
there are stirrings afoot,

88
00:05:25,880 --> 00:05:29,280
for an event held only once
every four years approaches.

89
00:05:29,660 --> 00:05:33,560
An event held at the center of
the world in Marijua itself.

90
00:05:34,240 --> 00:05:36,240
The Reverie, a council of kings.

91
00:05:36,660 --> 00:05:38,895
At this, the greatest of all councils,

92
00:05:39,020 --> 00:05:41,977
the rulers of fifty
kingdoms gather in one place

93
00:05:42,060 --> 00:05:45,220
to discuss and debate
matters of global importance,

94
00:05:45,440 --> 00:05:47,857
and decide upon their
plans for the future.

95
00:05:47,940 --> 00:05:51,940
But when these bunning and
off-centric rulers come face-to-face,

96
00:05:52,400 --> 00:05:55,960
matters never seen to proceed
as smoothly as one may hope.

97
00:05:58,820 --> 00:06:00,660
The war is over,

98
00:06:01,020 --> 00:06:06,440
and Tang Chin Jiao, that is to
say, Tang Sai, has yet to return.

99
00:06:08,580 --> 00:06:12,880
I fear that we will miss Reverie,
and we have many matters to discuss.

100
00:06:21,000 --> 00:06:23,137
Ma-ha-ha-ha-ha!

101
00:06:23,220 --> 00:06:25,797
Scar Kingdom, don't make me laugh.

102
00:06:25,880 --> 00:06:30,620
Now, how best to put that buffoon
Dalton in his place? What?

103
00:06:32,740 --> 00:06:35,320
What's that unappreciated face for?

104
00:06:35,760 --> 00:06:38,525
I'm saying I'll join you
as your ship's doctor.

105
00:06:38,900 --> 00:06:40,260
You're happy, right?

106
00:06:45,200 --> 00:06:46,837
Really? I can come?

107
00:06:46,920 --> 00:06:49,500
You can be my attendant, how about it?

108
00:06:50,180 --> 00:06:51,220
I'd love to.

109
00:06:51,480 --> 00:06:52,760
Thank you, Viola-san.

110
00:06:53,340 --> 00:06:55,120
Oh, this sounds exciting.

111
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:00,500
Ah, King Rick.

112
00:07:00,860 --> 00:07:03,600
I already turned down
my battleship escort.

113
00:07:04,140 --> 00:07:07,017
Say, why don't we travel
to the Holy Land together?

114
00:07:07,100 --> 00:07:09,806
Oh, do you think this
is some kind of holiday?

115
00:07:10,160 --> 00:07:11,748
And what's wrong with that?

116
00:07:22,580 --> 00:07:24,420
I'm sorry. I can't.

117
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:25,560
I'm too scared.

118
00:07:26,980 --> 00:07:29,000
Luffy-sama made a promise to me.

119
00:07:29,360 --> 00:07:31,478
He promised that when we meet again,

120
00:07:31,580 --> 00:07:34,580
he would take me to the
real forest on the surface.

121
00:07:35,980 --> 00:07:39,177
And I don't doubt Luffy-kun
will take you anywhere you wish.

122
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:40,777
But this isn't a long journey.

123
00:07:40,860 --> 00:07:43,820
We are only traveling to
Mary Joy, directly above.

124
00:07:49,480 --> 00:07:51,580
Oh, this won't do it.

125
00:07:51,760 --> 00:07:55,701
Father, shall we not just let
Shirahoshi sit this one out, Merde?

126
00:07:56,220 --> 00:07:58,514
Yeah, she doesn't need to go in person.

127
00:07:58,640 --> 00:08:03,460
We have plenty of signatures for our
petition to re-locate Fishman Island. Mambo!

128
00:08:03,860 --> 00:08:06,717
To leave her behind will
be not allowed to say

129
00:08:06,800 --> 00:08:10,340
that we do not trust the
humans or want them to.

130
00:08:11,440 --> 00:08:14,499
Shirahoshi, what did the
Star Hat Pirates teach you?

131
00:08:15,880 --> 00:08:19,780
This council is our chance to
fulfill our mother Otohime's wish.

132
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:21,140
Let us go together.

133
00:08:25,940 --> 00:08:27,580
A little of a starboard.

134
00:08:29,760 --> 00:08:31,260
Sure, like this.

135
00:08:32,000 --> 00:08:33,080
A little more.

136
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:36,700
Hey, hey, hey, put a
little more effort into it.

137
00:08:36,840 --> 00:08:39,277
Are you trying to sink us? Shut up.

138
00:08:39,360 --> 00:08:41,897
If you hadn't leapt off from
the top of Zoe like that,

139
00:08:41,980 --> 00:08:45,540
we wouldn't be all so
rattled, idiot. Thank you.

140
00:08:45,780 --> 00:08:48,780
I am reflecting on how
wonderful it is to be alive.

141
00:08:48,880 --> 00:08:50,780
I won't forget this.

142
00:08:55,300 --> 00:08:56,130
Wow!

143
00:08:56,213 --> 00:08:57,480
We're really on the sea!

144
00:08:58,380 --> 00:09:03,240
This big, heavy boat is
just floating along! Huh?

145
00:09:03,500 --> 00:09:05,382
What are you doing on the board?

146
00:09:06,000 --> 00:09:07,480
Carrot! Yoo-hoo!

147
00:09:08,420 --> 00:09:09,880
Carrot? Why are you?

148
00:09:10,040 --> 00:09:11,520
I decided to come along.

149
00:09:12,200 --> 00:09:13,080
Crush!

150
00:09:13,660 --> 00:09:14,880
Gar! Nami!

151
00:09:15,460 --> 00:09:16,640
Crush!

152
00:09:17,520 --> 00:09:18,350
Gar!

153
00:09:18,433 --> 00:09:19,263
Chopper! Crush!

154
00:09:19,960 --> 00:09:20,790
Gar!

155
00:09:21,260 --> 00:09:22,620
Baron Corpse!

156
00:09:22,980 --> 00:09:23,940
Crush!

157
00:09:24,520 --> 00:09:27,157
I'm afraid we'll just have
to turn this ship around.

158
00:09:27,240 --> 00:09:28,416
Don't turn back now!

159
00:09:28,720 --> 00:09:30,308
Wanda will be really angry.

160
00:09:30,480 --> 00:09:34,160
I just wanted to go on
an adventure for once.

161
00:09:34,660 --> 00:09:35,860
This isn't a game.

162
00:09:36,220 --> 00:09:38,337
Please, I'll do anything.

163
00:09:38,420 --> 00:09:40,677
Just take me with you.

164
00:09:40,760 --> 00:09:42,657
I won't get in the way.

165
00:09:42,740 --> 00:09:44,737
Look, I've brought lunch.

166
00:09:44,820 --> 00:09:46,437
Some juice, a snack.

167
00:09:46,520 --> 00:09:48,177
Spare clothes, and.

168
00:09:48,260 --> 00:09:50,537
The ocean really is.

169
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,637
A wonderland.

170
00:09:52,720 --> 00:09:54,997
It's not a land at all.

171
00:09:55,080 --> 00:09:56,537
It's the opposite of land.

172
00:09:56,620 --> 00:09:59,260
I've never been on a sleepover before.

173
00:10:00,800 --> 00:10:02,697
Oh well, it'll be fine.

174
00:10:02,780 --> 00:10:05,360
Yep, thank you. I'll be.

175
00:10:07,660 --> 00:10:09,740
Why are you eating my carrot?

176
00:10:10,420 --> 00:10:11,440
My neck!

177
00:10:12,960 --> 00:10:14,340
Pat her head, Luffy!

178
00:10:21,200 --> 00:10:22,460
That was close.

179
00:10:22,820 --> 00:10:23,780
I almost died.

180
00:10:24,420 --> 00:10:25,980
Luffy almost got killed.

181
00:10:26,940 --> 00:10:28,587
Well, she's used to a fight.

182
00:10:29,280 --> 00:10:30,277
Where the...

183
00:10:30,360 --> 00:10:33,242
When did you get all the
way up there, Pedro-san?

184
00:10:35,980 --> 00:10:37,000
I'm hungry.

185
00:10:37,260 --> 00:10:38,201
Let's have food.

186
00:10:38,440 --> 00:10:39,558
Somebody make food.

187
00:10:39,840 --> 00:10:41,428
Uh-oh, you're all hopeless.

188
00:10:41,520 --> 00:10:44,157
I'll go make something
to keep watch, will you?

189
00:10:44,240 --> 00:10:47,040
It'll cost you 5,000 penny each.

190
00:10:47,520 --> 00:10:48,980
Wait, wait, wait, wait.

191
00:10:49,740 --> 00:10:51,960
That's like all of my allowance.

192
00:10:52,580 --> 00:10:53,992
What are you suggesting?

193
00:10:56,060 --> 00:10:57,825
This is a pretty big headline.

194
00:10:58,460 --> 00:10:59,540
I'll make it.

195
00:11:01,000 --> 00:11:05,240
A location shrouded in mystery
for decades is finally discovered.

196
00:11:05,360 --> 00:11:11,220
Baltigo, headquarters of the
Revolutionary Army, lies in ruins.
